==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6~18 seconds<sup>180f~540f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 7.33~12.67 seconds<sup>220f~380f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The biggest threat in this stage are the Dagshunds, due to their one knockback and fairly high health. Using four meatshields, [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and units with [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack]] ([[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] works the best here, and if high enough leveled, can carry the stage) will secure you a victory. Since the first Dagshund spawns after 20 seconds, Worker [[Cat Combo]]s are strongly recommended.

However, there is a chance that enough Doges and Snaches will spawn before the first Dagshund spawns to fill the enemy limit. If that happens, you can easily stall the peons for max money using something like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] to make this stage even easier.

